<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6041"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Vazquez, Maria Luisa, 62, of 339 Federal St., Allentown, died Wednesday in Allentown Hospital. She was employed by the former Quaker Shoe Corp., Allentown, for 10 yrs. until retiring in 1969. Born in Cidra, PR, she was a daughter of the late Reyez and Modesta &#40;Negron&#41; Otero.  <BR> <BR>Survivors: Daughter, Carmen L. Reyes of Allentown; sons, Osvaldo, with whom she resided, Jose L. of Allentown and Luis A. of Whitehall Township; sisters, Gloria Vasquez of Bridgeport, CT, and ------ <BR> <BR>Petra Otero---- <BR> <BR>of Cidra; brother, Juan Otero of Caguas, PR; 9 grandchildren and 10 great-grandchildren. Weber Funeral Home, 1619 Hamilton St., Allentown. The Morning Call, Allentown, PA, Jun 8, 1989<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6041-->
<!--Post: 6042--><!--Time: 1107490058-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6042"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ciajoe<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ciajoe<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 8:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nope. This is Petra here:  <BR><a href="http://plaza.wichita.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodisplay.asp?ID=755" target=_top>http://plaza.wichita.edu/heroines/Heroine/biodispl ay.asp?ID=755</a> <BR> <BR>Tina mentioned is probably &#34;Christana&#34; listed on  <BR>that link.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6042-->
<!--Post: 6067--><!--Time: 1107519113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6067"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bakerwood<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bakerwood<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have known Christine for many years and have never known here as &#34;Tina&#34;. And the family is extremely Anglo-Caucasion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6067-->
<!--Post: 6068--><!--Time: 1107519666-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6068"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 4:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Petra Tasheff is honored with a <b>BRICK</b>???? <BR> <BR>HUH?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6068-->
<!--Post: 6080--><!--Time: 1107529038-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6080"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bakerwood<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bakerwood<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/10318357.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/10318357.htm</a> <BR> <BR>Topsail,  Have a look here.  It goes a bit further to explain how one can be &#34;honored with a brick&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6080-->
<!--Post: 6240--><!--Time: 1107626422-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6240"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 10:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bakerwood, I tried accessing the link above and it says the article cannot be found &#40;wouldn&#39;t surprise me if WPD had something to do that&#41;.  So, tell me about the brick.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6240-->
<!--Post: 6333--><!--Time: 1107703604-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6333"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bakerwood<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bakerwood<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 7:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK has told police he knew a Hispanic female named Petra, who had a younger sister named Tina. Some folks, in the search for a Puerto Rico connection were speculating about whether those two women are Petra and Christine Tasheff, sisters whose names appear on commemorative bricks on WSU&#39;s &#34;Plaza of Heroines.&#34;  The Plaza is a memorial walk-way at the university.  The Tasheffs of Wichita are Not Puerto Rican.  They are, as I said, Severely Anglo-Caucasian.   <BR>So, this is a grasping at straws thing here that has happened. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6333-->
<!--Post: 6341--><!--Time: 1107711347-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6341"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 9:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My original post is not in reference to the WSU Plaza of Heroines. Petra is a very common name in Puerto Rico as is Otero. However, my research was based upon Joe and Julie&#39;s background near San Juan, Joe&#39;s six years in the Panama Canal Zone and his service with the &#34;Inter-American Air Force&#34; which was a controversial US effort to train latin troops to serve our purposes in latin countries.  <BR> <BR>There are still many people that believe the latin soldiers we trained in these programs committed assassinations and torture in Cuba, the Dominican Republic and other countries. I was trying to determine whether or not there may be a &#34;revenge&#34; aspect to Joe and his family&#39;s murders.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6341-->
<!--Post: 6604--><!--Time: 1107906402-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6604"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie <BR> <BR>This human rights organization has massive amounts of information on the School of the Americas. <a href="http://www.soaw.org/new/" target=_top>http://www.soaw.org/new/</a> <BR> <BR>A searchable database on &#42;graduates&#42; not instructors. <a href="http://www.soaw.org/new/grads_search.php" target=_top>http://www.soaw.org/new/grads_search.php</a> <BR> <BR>Link to declassified interrogation manuals used. <a href="http://www.soaw.org/new/article.php?id=98" target=_top>http://www.soaw.org/new/article.php?id=98</a> <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6604-->
